WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.200
When dealing with a bite from an animal or even another person,

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:07.600
your two main concerns are managing the bleeding and preventing infection.

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:12.960
It is also important to remember that certain mammals, like raccoons, skunks, and bats,

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:17.440
can transmit rabies through a bite, which is a very serious medical situation.

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:20.879
If someone is bitten, follow these steps to provide care.

00:00:20.879 --> 00:00:25.280
First, ensure the scene is safe so you don't become the next victim.

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:29.840
Second, wash the wound gently with soap and water to help prevent infection.

00:00:30.639 --> 00:00:35.360
Third, control any bleeding by applying firm, direct pressure.

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:39.840
You can also apply an ice pack to the area to help reduce pain and swelling.

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:41.680
If the bite breaks the skin at all,

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:45.200
the person needs to contact a healthcare provider for further treatment.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:50.160
However, you should call 911 immediately if there is severe bleeding that won't stop,

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:54.000
if the person is still in danger, or if you have any reason to suspect

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.680
the animal might have rabies.

